president pedro castillo is swearing in  a new cabinet the third in only six  months the latest shake-up comes after  the interior and prime ministers  resigned this week  critics claim castillo only trusts an  inner circle of advisers operating  behind the scenes they're not appointed  ministers  this political crisis shows corruption  former prime minister mirita vasquez  made serious accusations that the  government is not fighting corruption we  have all our presidents questioned and  is generating an enormous mistrust  towards the authorities  most of peru's former presidents are  under investigation for corruption the  last presidential term was marked by a  series of political crisis that left the  south american nation with four  presidents in only five years  the attorney general has denounced  castillo for illegal sponsorship and  influence peddling the farmer and union  leader denies any allegation instead he  said he hasn't been trained to be  president but critics say that is  unacceptable  he should be prepared and especially in  such a dramatic situation with the  health economic and labor crisis  peru has regressed several points in its  poverty rates and this is an element  that is not for experiments we need  clear answers from our rulers  opinion polls say more than 60 percent  of peruvians disapprove of this  government many peruvians say that  castillo has a credibility problem that  he's not qualified for the job and the  country is adrift former prime minister  mirta vazquez says that castillo could  begin solving crucial issues by  surrounding himself with competent  people  the growing discontent appears to be  overshadowing some of his achievements  like the fight against the covet 19  pandemic at least 80 percent of the  target population has been vaccinated at  least  once we should change this man  immediately because he is ruining  everything economically there are no  jobs no sales  he really does not deserve to be there  he is totally incapable he proves it day  by day it's a shame this person is the  head of peru  lawmakers have to decide whether they  will approve the new cabinet but for now  many opponents say they are focusing  instead in paving the way to vacate him  mariana sanchez lima peru
 

